laurel 2892: GPU clock by demand, 300 <-> 600 MHz from GPLL0 (new iokit/Kernel/arm/LaurelGpuDcvs.cpp). Self-check before the UI: GPU temperature, clock read at 300 (GCC clock counter, CP counter next to it), MX+CX NOM vote through TopazRpm (held for the boot, never lowered), GPLL0 / 1, clock read at 600, CP fence, back to 300. Demand: busy >= 50 % over 50 ms or touch -> 600; below 20 % for 500 ms -> 300; thermal: no 600 from 90 C to 80 C (sensor 15). Watchdog: no fence progress for 1500 ms at 600 MHz -> 300 MHz, feature off. DDR: MCCC period register read; a vote only when it is below the wanted bus level and the RPM follows (LAUREL DDR line). Time per level a minute. The RedwoodGPU 5 s line is split in three: one log line ends after 255 bytes, so "GPU busy B %, core C MHz" never reached a log. Kill switch gpudcvs=0. Any failure: 300 MHz, GPU stays on.

